+    # AEMULATOR: the host must be able to DECODE everything the guest can ENCODE.
+    #
+    # cerealgenerator only emits marshal / reservedunmarshal / deepcopy / transform cases for
+    # features named here; everything else falls through UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE_MODULES into the SIZE
+    # table alone. A struct that can be sized but not decoded reaches
+    # reservedunmarshal_extension_struct()'s default: arm, which is abort() of the whole VMM. The
+    # host therefore HIDES such extensions from the guest (VkDecoderCerealGap.inc) rather than
+    # serving them — so every name missing from this list is an extension the guest is denied.
+    #
+    # Contents: everything Mesa KosmicKrisp advertises, plus everything the guest encoder's own
+    # SUPPORTED_FEATURES can emit, intersected with the vendored 1.3.269 registry, minus the
+    # deny-list below. Each name was checked individually against this generator before landing.
+    #
+    # DELIBERATELY ABSENT — do NOT "fix" these by adding them:
+    #   VK_KHR_push_descriptor          vkCmdPushDescriptorSetWithTemplateKHR passes an opaque
+    #                                   const void* interpreted through a VkDescriptorUpdateTemplate.
+    #                                   gfxstream handles templates via DescriptorSetVirtualization;
+    #                                   the codegen cannot marshal it.
+    #   VK_EXT_extended_dynamic_state3  vkCmdSetViewportSwizzleNV takes const VkViewportSwizzleNV*,
+    #                                   and reg.py declares each type exactly once, under the FIRST
+    #                                   feature that requires it. Without the NV extensions that type
+    #                                   is never declared: a hard build break.
+    #   VK_EXT_multi_draw               its commands take a stride-strided array, and the generator
+    #                                   has no stride concept at all (grep -rn stride
+    #                                   codegen/scripts/cereal/*.py is empty). It would marshal with
+    #                                   sizeof() and silently corrupt the stream.
+    #   VK_EXT_mutable_descriptor_type  EXT/VALVE registry aliases under the same declare-once rule.
+    #   ray tracing / video / *AMDX* / provisional beta-guarded extensions — a beta guard compiles
+    #                                   the bodies OUT while the size table still sizes them, which
+    #                                   silently re-creates the exact gap this list exists to close.
+    #
+    # Those four remain in VkDecoderCerealGap.inc on purpose and stay hidden from the guest. That is
+    # why gap ∩ host does not reach zero, and why kCerealGapExtensionsKeptAnyway cannot be emptied.
